{"table":"nodes","ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/circuit.classical_positive","record":{"id":"circuit.classical_positive","kind":"goal","label":"Alternative finite-temperature bounded synthesis input","status":"unverified","source_id":"circuit-r2-26-source-positive","locator":"07-positive-temperature.tex:739–788; prop:classical-near-optimum-positive-temperature","statement":"Under the independent finite-temperature input family, for every ε>0 and η_H>0 there is a finite bounded odd trigonometric exclusion formula with centered output m_col, |m_col|≤1, E(m_col)≥P_*−ε, and 0<p_H<η_H. One positive helper type is reserved per depth, every propagation excludes current/ancestor/helper colors, and all finite data are independent of D,n,J.","assumption_ids":["circuit.positive_input"],"evidence_ids":[],"citation_ids":["circuit-r2-26-cite-classical-positive"],"boundary":"This is an alternative to the primary zero-temperature construction. It is a separate query root and is not an additional prerequisite of the primary route. It uses the same later bounded approximation, exclusion, synthesis and seed-removal machinery."},"usage":{"record_ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/circuit.classical_positive","paper_focus":[],"paper_memberships":[{"stage":"long","subgraph_ref":"sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json/support/0.3.1/69473417dc487cafa5e2e39b3168d2c4a8bffdad2e91b6e486de48f122dda071","roles":["mapped_claim"]}],"direct_passages":[{"stage":"long","passage_ref":"sha256:9e0f6d255eb0a116c513a0c11e94d28559f0a429ef365c3137bb4ff3b6a061d6/papers/long.md/sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json/passages/alternative-assembly","anchor":"alternative-assembly","mapping_ref":"sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json","mapping_field":"claim_ids"}]},"aligned_passages":[{"stage":"long","passage_ref":"sha256:9e0f6d255eb0a116c513a0c11e94d28559f0a429ef365c3137bb4ff3b6a061d6/papers/long.md/sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json/passages/alternative-assembly","anchor":"alternative-assembly","mapping_ref":"sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json","mapping_field":"claim_ids","text":"\nAfter clipping and bounded approximation, the result enters the same\nsynthesis and seed-removal route as the primary construction. Its source\ndependencies and fixed-temperature choice of parameters remain separate\nfrom the retained zero-temperature formal interfaces.\n[OpenAI (2026b), Appendix A][q-positive].\n\n<a id=\"temperature-route-comparison\"></a>\n\n### 11.1.1 Where the temperature routes meet\n\nBoth routes produce a bounded finite classical calculation whose rooted\nenergy is close to $P_*$. They reach that common input by different\ntheorems and different finite approximations.\n\n**Variational input and support.** The zero-temperature route fixes an\nattained minimizer $\\gamma\\in\\mathcal U$ with terminal value $|x|$ and\nuses full relative Stieltjes support on $[0,1)$. The positive-temperature\nroute fixes a finite $\\beta_0>1$ and its Parisi probability measure, with\nterminal value $\\beta_0^{-1}\\log(2\\cosh\\beta_0x)$; it uses Lopatto's\ninterval-support result on $[0,q_{\\beta_0}]$.\n\n**Scalar error.** Before discretization, the zero-temperature loss is at\nmost $1-T$ for $T<1$. The positive-temperature loss is at most\n$$\n(1/4+\\log2)/\\beta_0+(q_{\\beta_0}-T),\\qquad T<q_{\\beta_0}.\n$$\n\n**Finite energy.** In the zero-temperature route, a first-chaos projection\nidentifies the explicit Gaussian coefficient sum with\n$\\operatorname{Re}\\langle F_N,\\mathsf L F_N\\rangle$. The alternative\nroute first calculates finite-degree messages and edge energy, then uses\na rooted norm and occupation argument.\n\n**Order of approximation.** At zero temperature, fix $T$ before refining\nthe scalar mesh, and choose a finite mesh before regularization and synthesis.\nAt positive temperature, fix $\\beta_0,T,\\delta,L$ for the message degree\nlimit, then refine $\\delta$ at fixed $\\beta_0,T$.\n\nBoth routes then use the same bounded approximation, exclusions, seeded\nsynthesis, seed removal and fixed-word transfer. The quantum construction\nis shared; its classical input has been supplied independently.\n\nHere the displayed positive-temperature estimate is exactly the one\nderived above, rather than an assertion of convergence of zero-temperature\nsupports. One can choose $\\beta_0$ and $T$ finitely for the required\nerror and then stop. The later circuit argument needs that finite\nchoice; it never asks for a joint limit of the temperature, message\nmesh, graph degree and circuit depth. [OpenAI (2026b), Appendix A,\nProposition “The independent positive-temperature construction”][q-positive];\n[§6][q-assembly].\n","span":{"start_byte":205160,"end_byte":207667,"start_line":4431,"end_line":4481},"paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/long?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&paper=long&passage=alternative-assembly","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&paper=long&passage=alternative-assembly"}],"lenses":{"prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&view=arguments&node=circuit.classical_positive&assumptions=true","consumers":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&view=arguments&node=circuit.classical_positive&direction=consumers&assumptions=true","direct_passages":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&node=circuit.classical_positive&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&node=circuit.classical_positive&relation=prerequisites"},"relations":[{"family":"arguments","id":"field:66b0e39163e6a25c643642defb37b1ad4f237342ec8114e5d078899eb8896d4a","from":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/circuit.classical_positive","to":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/circuit.positive_input","kind":"assumption_ids","semantic_class":"explicit_assumption_reference","derived":true,"owner_ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/circuit.classical_positive","source_field":"assumption_ids"},{"family":"arguments","id":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/edges/%5B%22circuit.classical_positive%22%2C%22circuit.bounded_trigonometric%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","from":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/circuit.classical_positive","to":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/circuit.bounded_trigonometric","kind":"supports","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","derived":false,"record_ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/edges/%5B%22circuit.classical_positive%22%2C%22circuit.bounded_trigonometric%22%2C%22supports%22%5D"},{"family":"arguments","id":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/edges/%5B%22circuit.classical_positive%22%2C%22circuit.color_exclusion%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","from":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/circuit.classical_positive","to":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/circuit.color_exclusion","kind":"supports","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","derived":false,"record_ref":"sha256:c94